title: Next Steps
description: Where to go after completing the Getting Started guides
---

Congratulations on completing the Getting Started guides! You now have a working Pika installation and understand the basics of creating agents. This page will help you decide where to go next based on your goals.

## Choose Your Path

### I Want to Build Production Applications

If you're ready to build real applications for your users:

{% card title="Implement Real Authentication" icon="warning" %}
Replace the mock authentication provider with a real one. This is **critical** before deploying to production.

[Authentication Guide →](/how-to/authentication/)
{% /card %}

{% card title="Configure Access Control" icon="setting" %}
Set up user types and chat app visibility to control who can access what.

[Access Control Guide →](/how-to/access-control/)
{% /card %}

{% card title="Deploy to AWS" icon="rocket" %}
Learn how to deploy your Pika instance to AWS for production use.

[AWS Deployment Guide →](/how-to/deployment/aws/)
{% /card %}

{% card title="Set Up CI/CD" icon="approve-check" %}
Automate your deployment pipeline with continuous integration and deployment.

[CI/CD Guide →](/how-to/deployment/cicd/)
{% /card %}

### I Want to Learn More About Pika

If you want to deepen your understanding of how Pika works:

{% card title="Explore Capabilities" icon="star" %}
Discover all the features and capabilities Pika offers for building intelligent chat applications.

[Capabilities Overview →](/capabilities/)
{% /card %}

{% card title="Understand the Architecture" icon="puzzle" %}
Learn how Pika works under the hood, including AWS infrastructure, session management, and the self-correcting loop.

[Concepts & Architecture →](/concepts/)
{% /card %}

{% card title="Read the Design Philosophy" icon="information" %}
Understand why Pika was built and the problems it solves.

[Why Pika →](/why/)
{% /card %}

### I Want to Build Advanced Features

If you're ready to add sophisticated capabilities to your agents:

{% card title="Add Tools to Your Agents" icon="setting" %}
Learn how to give your agents access to external APIs, databases, and services using inline tools.

[Inline Tools Guide →](/how-to/tools/inline-tools/)
{% /card %}

{% card title="Integrate with MCP" icon="puzzle" %}
Connect to Model Context Protocol servers to give your agents access to external tools and data sources.

[MCP Integration Guide →](/how-to/tools/mcp/)
{% /card %}

{% card title="Enable Multi-Agent Collaboration" icon="star" %}
Create systems where multiple specialized agents work together to solve complex problems.

[Multi-Agent Guide →](/how-to/agents/multi-agent/)
{% /card %}

{% card title="Build Custom Web Components" icon="pencil" %}
Create custom UI components to render rich, interactive content in chat responses.

[Web Components Guide →](/how-to/customization/web-components/)
{% /card %}

### I Want to Improve Agent Quality

If you want to make your agents more reliable and accurate:

{% card title="Enable Self-Correcting Responses" icon="approve-check" %}
Use Pika's self-correcting loop to automatically verify and improve agent responses.

[Self-Correcting Guide →](/how-to/intelligence/self-correcting/)
{% /card %}

{% card title="Use Answer Verification" icon="information" %}
Configure independent verification of agent responses before they reach users.

[Answer Verification Guide →](/how-to/intelligence/verification/)
{% /card %}

{% card title="Set Up LLM Feedback" icon="star" %}
Enable AI-generated feedback on chat sessions to identify improvement opportunities.

[LLM Feedback Guide →](/how-to/intelligence/feedback/)
{% /card %}

{% card title="Master Instruction Engineering" icon="pencil" %}
Learn how to write effective instructions and use Pika's instruction assistance tools.

[Instruction Engineering →](/how-to/intelligence/instructions/)
{% /card %}

### I Want to Customize the Experience

If you want to tailor Pika to your brand and requirements:

{% card title="Customize the UI" icon="setting" %}
Modify the chat interface to match your brand and design requirements.

[UI Customization Guide →](/how-to/customization/ui/)
{% /card %}

{% card title="Configure User Memory" icon="information" %}
Set up persistent user memory so agents remember context across sessions.

[User Memory Guide →](/how-to/data/user-memory/)
{% /card %}

{% card title="Manage Sessions" icon="puzzle" %}
Learn how to configure and work with chat sessions.

[Session Management Guide →](/how-to/data/sessions/)
{% /card %}

{% card title="Override Default Features" icon="setting" %}
Customize feature behavior for specific chat apps.

[Feature Overrides Guide →](/how-to/customization/feature-overrides/)
{% /card %}

## Learning Path Recommendations

### For Product Managers and Decision Makers

1. [Why Pika](/why/) - Understand the value proposition
2. [Who Is Pika For](/why/who-is-pika-for/) - See if it fits your use case
3. [Capabilities Overview](/capabilities/) - Learn what you can build
4. [Pika vs Other Solutions](/why/comparison/) - Compare alternatives

### For Developers New to AI Agents

1. [What Are AI Agents](/concepts/ai-agents/) - Understand the basics
2. [How Pika Works](/concepts/how-it-works/) - Learn the architecture
3. [Agent Development Basics](/how-to/agents/basics/) - Start building
4. [Tools and Integration](/how-to/tools/) - Add capabilities

### For Experienced AI Developers

1. [Agent-as-Config Philosophy](/concepts/agent-as-config/) - Understand the approach
2. [Multi-Agent Orchestration](/how-to/agents/multi-agent/) - Advanced patterns
3. [Self-Correcting Loop](/concepts/self-correcting/) - Quality improvements
4. [Direct Agent Invocation](/how-to/agents/direct-invocation/) - Programmatic access

### For DevOps and Infrastructure Teams

1. [AWS Architecture](/concepts/architecture/aws/) - Understand infrastructure
2. [AWS Deployment](/how-to/deployment/aws/) - Deploy to production
3. [Security Architecture](/concepts/security/) - Security model
4. [Monitoring and Traces](/how-to/operations/monitoring/) - Operational tooling

## Common Next Tasks

### Set Up a Real Use Case

1. Identify a specific use case (customer support, internal knowledge base, etc.)
2. Design your agent's capabilities and knowledge requirements
3. Implement necessary tools for data access
4. Configure authentication and access control
5. Test thoroughly with real users
6. Deploy to production with monitoring

### Integrate with Existing Systems

1. Map your existing authentication to Pika's user types
2. Create tools to access your databases and APIs
3. Build custom web components for your data types
4. Configure access control based on your org structure
5. Embed Pika chat into your existing applications

### Build a Multi-Agent System

1. Identify specialized domains (e.g., sales, support, technical)
2. Create agents for each domain with specific instructions
3. Configure agent collaboration patterns
4. Test coordination between agents
5. Monitor performance and iterate

